{
  "type": "doc",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "center",
        "level": 1
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Build an Advanced Reranking RAG"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left",
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Introduction"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Large Language Models (LLMs) are powerful tools but are known to sometimes \"hallucinate,\" producing incorrect or misleading information. This blog post explores how to mitigate this issue by using Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG), specifically with an advanced reranking system to improve accuracy."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "RAG combines information retrieval with in-context learning to deliver more reliable answers. The goal is to enhance the quality of responses generated by LLMs by grounding them in relevant external knowledge. This is done by retrieving pertinent document segments and including them in the LLM's prompt."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In this post, we will detail how to construct a RAG system that leverages reranking to optimize the relevance of retrieved documents, ensuring that the LLM has access to the most pertinent information. We will build this system using "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Llama-Index"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Llama 3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", and "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Qdrant"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "You'll learn about vector embeddings, the reranking process, and how to integrate these components for improved question answering accuracy. Let's dive into building an advanced RAG system that minimizes hallucination and maximizes the quality of LLM outputs. Next, we'll explore the concept of RAG in greater detail."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left",
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Section 1: Topic Overview"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In this blog post, we're diving into the world of advanced RAG (Retrieval Augmented Generation) systems. RAG is a technique to enhance the knowledge and reliability of Large Language Models (LLMs) by providing them with relevant external information."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "At its core, RAG combines two main processes: "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Retrieval"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", where the system finds relevant pieces of information from a knowledge base, and "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Augmentation"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", where this retrieved information is added to the prompt given to the LLM. It's like giving the LLM a cheat sheet to answer questions more accurately."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A crucial element in advanced RAG is "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "reranking"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". Imagine sifting through hundreds of documents \u2013 not all are equally relevant. Reranking helps to prioritize the most pertinent documents, ensuring that the LLM focuses on the best possible information. This drastically improves the quality of the answers generated by the LLM."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "blockquote",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
            "textAlign": null
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Reranking is like having a smart librarian who knows exactly which books you need, even if the library is huge!"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In the upcoming sections, we\u2019ll explore the specifics of building an advanced reranking RAG system using Llama-Index, Llama 3, and Qdrant. You'll learn how these technologies work together to create a robust and accurate question-answering system."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left",
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Important Components"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Building an advanced reranking RAG system involves several key components working together. Understanding these components is crucial before diving into the implementation. Each part plays a specific role in retrieving and refining information to provide accurate answers. Let's explore the core elements that make up this system."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "First, there's the "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Vector Store"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", such as "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Qdrant"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". This database stores document segments as vector embeddings, enabling efficient similarity searches. Next is the "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Embedding Model"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", which transforms text into numerical vectors. For instance, "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "FastEmbed"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " can create these embeddings."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Also, the "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "LLM (Language Model)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", like "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Llama 3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", is crucial for generating responses. Then we need the "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Reranker Module"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", which improves the relevance of retrieved documents. "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "SentenceTransformerRerank"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " is a great example for this task. Finally, the "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Query Engine"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " integrates all these components for question answering."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "blockquote",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
            "textAlign": null
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Each component in the RAG system is vital, and optimizing them ensures that the system delivers relevant and accurate information."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "With a grasp of these components, we can move on to discuss how to put them together. In the next section, we\u2019ll explore the technical stack in detail, explaining how "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Llama-Index"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Qdrant"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", and "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Llama 3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " integrate to create a powerful RAG system."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left",
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "How-To Steps"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Building an advanced reranking RAG system involves several key steps. By following these steps, you can effectively integrate Llama-Index, Llama 3, and Qdrant to create a powerful question answering system that leverages private data. Here's a guide to help you through the process:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "bulletList",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "attrs": {
                "textAlign": "left"
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Install required libraries: Start by installing the necessary libraries using "
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "code"
                    }
                  ],
                  "text": "pip install -r requirements.txt"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ". This includes Llama-Index, Qdrant client, and other dependencies."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "attrs": {
                "textAlign": "left"
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Load and process documents: Load your data using "
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "code"
                    }
                  ],
                  "text": "SimpleDirectoryReader"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " from Llama-Index. Ensure your documents are properly formatted and accessible."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "attrs": {
                "textAlign": "left"
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Set up the LLM: Instantiate Llama 3 by logging in to Hugging Face and configuring the tokenizer and model settings. System prompts are used for accurately answering based on the instructions and context."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "attrs": {
                "textAlign": "left"
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Instantiate Vector Store and Load the Vector Embeddings: By setting up the vector store and loading the vector embeddings we are allowing the system to have a way to store embeddings."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "attrs": {
                "textAlign": "left"
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Set up reranking: Use "
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "code"
                    }
                  ],
                  "text": "SentenceTransformerRerank"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " to rerank the retrieved documents. Configure it to select the top "
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "code"
                    }
                  ],
                  "text": "n"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " most relevant documents."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "attrs": {
                "textAlign": "left"
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Create the query engine: Initialize the query engine with the reranking module. Set the similarity top_k parameter to define how many documents to retrieve initially."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "blockquote",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
            "textAlign": null
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Tip: Regularly update your vector embeddings to keep your RAG system's knowledge base current and accurate."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "By following these steps, you can set up a robust RAG system that improves the accuracy and relevance of LLM-generated responses. Next, we'll test the system with a few example questions."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left",
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Common Issues"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "When building an advanced Reranking RAG system, it's common to encounter a few stumbling blocks. One frequent issue is the tendency for the retriever to pull in irrelevant or noisy context, even with embedding-based similarity. This can significantly dilute the quality of information passed to the LLM, leading to less accurate and coherent responses. Addressing this is critical for a functional system."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Another problem is related to choosing the right reranking model. Models like "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "code"
            }
          ],
          "text": "cross-encoder/ms-marco-MiniLM-L-2-v2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " are good starting points, but they might not be optimal for every domain or use case. Experimenting with different rerankers and fine-tuning them on your specific data can yield substantial improvements. Also, ensure that your "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "similarity_top_k"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " value balances precision and recall."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Misconceptions also play a role. Many beginners assume that simply throwing more data at the RAG system will solve accuracy issues. However, without a robust reranking mechanism, the LLM might still struggle to sift through the noise. It\u2019s crucial to remember that "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "quality is always better than quantity"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " when it comes to context."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "blockquote",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
            "textAlign": null
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Takeaway: Don't underestimate the reranking step! It's the key to filtering irrelevant context and providing the LLM with the best possible information."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left",
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Conclusion"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In conclusion, we've explored Build an Advanced Reranking RAG in detail. "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "We hope this guide helps you apply these concepts effectively. "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Remember to practice regularly "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "and refer back to this guide whenever needed."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}